e first 4 cards of “More recipes” in DATA, each with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite)\\n• Share: “SHARE THIS ON:” · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram\\n---\\nLINKS\\n---\\n→ Blog (nav) → 03_Blog\\n→ recommended recipe “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus” → 02_Recipe\\n---\\n05_Contact\\n---\\nGoal: Send the team a message.\\n---\\nMUST INCLUDE\\n---\\n• Contact form: “Contact us” · NAME (placeholder “Enter your name...”) · EMAIL ADDRESS (“Your email address...”) · SUBJECT (“Enter subject...”) · ENQUIRY TYPE: Advertising (Icon_Chevron_Down) · MESSAGE (“Enter your message...”) · “Submit” · Photo_Chef_Contact\\n• Footer: see DATA (Footer)\\n• Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Contact · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram\\n• Newsletter: “Deliciousness to your inbox” · copy (see DATA) · email field “Your email address...” · “Subscribe” · Decor_Subscribe_Vegetables · Decor_Subscribe_Leaf · Decor_Subscribe_Salad\\n• Recommended recipes: “Check out the delicious recipes” · the first 4 cards of “More recipes” in DATA, each with photo, title, time (Icon_Timer), category (Icon_Fork_Knife) and favorite (Icon_Favorite)\\n---\\nLINKS\\n---\\n→ Home (nav) → 01_Home\\n→ recommended recipe “Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus” → 02_Recipe\\n---\\nNavigation structure\\n---\\n• Header on all 5 frames: Logo_Foodieland, then Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us, then Facebook, Twitter and Instagram. Current: Home on 01, Recipes on 02, Blog on 03 and 04, Contact on 05. How the current item looks is yours.\\n• Footer on all 5 frames. Newsletter card on all 5 frames.\\n• Flow: 01_Home → recipe card → 02_Recipe. Blog → 03_Blog → article → 04_Blog_Post. Contact → 05_Contact. Recommended-recipe cards on 02, 04 and 05 lead to 02_Recipe for the fried rice; other cards are entry only.\\n• Entry only (no frame): Recipes (the list) and About us in the nav, social logos, View Recipes, View All Categories, category tiles, other recipe cards, favorites, Learn More, Instagram post actions, Visit Our Instagram, PRINT, SHARE, play, checkboxes, Other Recipe / Tasty Recipes items, promo card, search, pagination, other articles, form fields, Submit, Subscribe.\\n---\\nFixed data & copy\\n---\\nUse these values verbatim.\\n---\\nHome copy\\n---\\nFeatured: Crispy outside, juicy inside and coated in a sticky, spicy glaze — these wings are ready in 30 minutes and disappear even faster.\\nSimple and tasty recipes: Quick, everyday dishes with ingredients you can find at any supermarket.\\nChef promo: Step-by-step recipes, clear timings and tips from our cooks help you make restaurant-quality food at home.\\nInstagram: Follow us for daily recipe ideas, behind-the-scenes cooking and photos from our community.\\nMore recipes: Fresh ideas for breakfast, lunch and dinner — pick one and get cooking.\\n---\\nSimple and tasty recipes (01, in order; ♥ = favorited)\\n---\\nBig and Juicy Wagyu Beef Cheeseburger · 30 Minutes · Western · ♥ (Photo_Wagyu_Cheeseburger)\\nFresh Lime Roasted Salmon with Ginger Sauce · 30 Minutes · Fish (Photo_Lime_Salmon)\\nStrawberry Oatmeal Pancake with Honey Syrup · 30 Minutes · Breakfast (Photo_Strawberry_Oatmeal_Pancake)\\nFresh and Healthy Mixed Mayonnaise Salad · 30 Minutes · Healthy · ♥ (Photo_Mayonnaise_Salad)\\nChicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese · 30 Minutes · Meat (Photo_Chicken_Meatballs)\\nFruity Pancake with Orange & Blueberry · 30 Minutes · Sweet · ♥ (Photo_Fruity_Pancake)\\nThe Best Easy One Pot Chicken and Rice · 30 Minutes · Snack (Photo_One_Pot_Chicken_Rice)\\nThe Creamiest Creamy Chicken and Bacon Pasta · 30 Minutes · Noodles (Photo_Creamy_Chicken_Bacon_Pasta)\\n---\\nMore recipes (01, in order; ♥ = favorited)\\n---\\nMixed Tropical Fruit Salad with Superfood Boosts · 30 Minutes · Healthy · ♥ (Photo_Tropical_Fruit_Salad)\\nBig and Juicy Wagyu Beef Cheeseburger · 30 Minutes · Western (Photo_Wagyu_Cheeseburger_Alt)\\nHealthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus · 30 Minutes · Healthy (Photo_Japanese_Fried_Rice)\\nCauliflower Walnut Vegetarian Taco Meat · 30 Minutes · Eastern (Photo_Cauliflower_Taco)\\nRainbow Chicken Salad with Almond Honey Mustard Dressing · 30 Minutes · Healthy · ♥ (Photo_Rainbow_Chicken_Salad)\\nBarbeque Spicy Sandwiches with Chips · 30 Minutes · Snack (Photo_Barbeque_Sandwiches)\\nFirecracker Vegan Lettuce Wraps - Spicy! · 30 Minutes · Vegan (Photo_Vegan_Lettuce_Wraps)\\nChicken Ramen Soup with Mushroom · 30 Minutes · Japanese · ♥ (Photo_Chicken_Ramen)\\n---\\nInstagram posts (01, in order)\\n---\\n1. Photo_Instagram_1 — The vegetable dishes need to have certain vitamins for those people\\n2. Photo_Instagram_2 — Sweet food can bring someone happiness, as long as they don’t eat too much\\n3. Photo_Instagram_3 — What do you do before you start cooking? Prepare the tools or the ingredients?\\n4. Photo_Instagram_4 — Steak is never wrong; it’s perfect if you want a romantic dinner\\nAll: Foodieland. · Tokyo, Japan · 1/3 · Liked by craig_love and 44,686 others · September 19\\n---\\nRecipe (02) · intro & nutrition\\n---\\nIntro: A quick weeknight fried rice that turns leftover rice into a light, healthy meal. Crisp asparagus, soft eggs and a simple soy-sesame sauce come together in one pan in about 30 minutes.\\nNutrition note: Values are per serving and approximate.\\n---\\nRecipe (02) · ingredients\\n---\\nFor main dish: 2 cups cooked jasmine rice, chilled overnight (checked) · 1 bunch asparagus, cut into 2 cm pieces · 2 eggs, beaten · 2 spring onions, thinly sliced · 1 tbsp neutral oil\\nFor the sauce: 2 tbsp soy sauce · 1 tsp sesame oil · 1 tsp mirin\\n---\\nRecipe (02) · directions\\n---\\n1. Prepare the ingredients — Cut the asparagus, slice the spring onions and beat the eggs. Mix the soy sauce, sesame oil and mirin in a small bowl. [Photo_Cooking_Step] Day-old rice works best: it is drier, so the grains fry separately instead of turning mushy. Break up any clumps before you start.\\n2. Cook the eggs and asparagus — Heat the oil in a wok over high heat. Scramble the eggs until just set, push them to the side, then stir-fry the asparagus for 2 minutes until bright green and still crisp.\\n3. Fry the rice and season — Add the rice and toss for 3–4 minutes until hot and lightly toasted. Pour over the sauce, fold in the eggs and spring onions, and serve right away.\\n---\\nArticles (03, in order)\\n---\\nAll dated 12 November 2021.\\n1. Crochet Projects for Noodle Lovers · Wade Warren (Photo_Chicken_Ramen, Avatar_Wade_Warren) — Our favourite slurpable noodle bowls, from quick ramen to slow-simmered broths.\\n2. 10 Vegetarian Recipes To Eat This Month · Robert Fox (Photo_Tropical_Fruit_Salad, Avatar_Robert_Fox) — Seasonal, meat-free dishes that are colourful, filling and easy to make.\\n3. Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef · Dianne Russell (Photo_Blog_Chef, Avatar_Dianne_Russell) — A working head chef on first jobs, long services and what it really takes.\\n4. Simple & Delicious Vegetarian Lasagna · Leslie Alexander (Photo_Vegetarian_Lasagna, Avatar_Leslie_Alexander) — Layers of roasted vegetables, rich tomato sauce and creamy béchamel.\\n5. Plantain and Pinto Stew with Aji Verde · Courtney Henry (Photo_Plantain_Stew, Avatar_Courtney_Henry) — A hearty one-pot stew finished with a bright, herby green sauce.\\n6. We’re Hiring a Communications Assistant! · Albert Flores (Photo_Hiring, Avatar_Albert_Flores) — Love food and words? Join our small team and help us tell more food stories.\\n---\\nBlog post (04) · header & Q1–Q2\\n---\\nIntro: We asked a working head chef about first jobs, long services and what it really takes to make it in a professional kitchen.\\nHow did you start out in the food industry? — I started washing dishes in a small family restaurant when I was sixteen. Watching the line cooks every night made me want to be on the other side of the pass, and after two years the chef finally let me prep vegetables.\\nWhat do you like most about your job? — The rhythm of service. Hours of preparation come down to a few intense minutes, and when a full dining room goes quiet because everyone is eating, it feels like the whole team has done something together.\\n---\\nBlog post (04) · Q3–Q5 & quote\\n---\\nDo you cook at home on your days off? — Yes, but simply. I cook the food I grew up with: rice, eggs and whatever vegetables look good at the market. Home cooking is where I remember why I love food. [Photo_Cooking_Step]\\nWhat would your advice be to young people looking to get their foot in the door? — Start anywhere and be the person who shows up early. Ask questions, taste everything and write down what you learn.\\nPull quote: “Technique can be taught; curiosity and reliability can’t.”\\nWhat is the biggest misconception that people have about being a professional chef? — That it is all creativity. Most of the job is consistency: making the same dish perfectly two hundred times a night, keeping the kitchen clean and looking after your team.\\n---\\nNewsletter (all frames)\\n---\\nDeliciousness to your inbox\\nGet new recipes and cooking tips in your inbox every week. No spam, unsubscribe anytime.\\nYour email address... · Subscribe\\n---\\nFooter (all frames)\\n---\\nLogo_Foodieland · “Simple, tasty recipes for every day.”\\nLinks: Recipes · Blog · Contact · About us\\n“© 2020 Foodieland. All rights reserved.” · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram\\n---\\nWhat is fixed · what is yours\\n---\\nFixed (given)\\n---\\n• Frame list and exact names\\n• Must-include content per frame (what, not how)\\n• Navigation structure and links\\n• All data and copy\\n• Brand colors #000000 and #E7F9FD, and Inter\\n• Media: wordmark, social logos, photos, category images, decorations, avatars, icons\\n• Default Button, default Text Field\\n---\\nYours (designer decides)\\n---\\n• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis on every page\\n• All other colors: neutrals, text, other backgrounds / surfaces, favorite / like color, links, error / disabled\\n• Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation\\n• All states: current nav item, favorited card, checked item, current page, focused field, hover\\n• Header, footer, featured recipe, category tile, recipe card, promo card, Instagram post, newsletter card, recipe meta, nutrition panel, ingredient checklist, direction step, article list item, sidebar lists, search bar, pagination, article layout, pull quote, form, select\\n• How photos and cut-outs are cropped and placed\\n---\\nHow it is evaluated\\n---\\nYour file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\\n---\\n1. Checklist coverage per frame\\n2. Data & copy accuracy\\n3. Flow & prototype completeness\\n4. Information hierarchy\\n5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system\\n6. Component reuse\\n7. State design (current nav, favorited, checked, current page)\\n---\\nDeliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 5 named frames, your components and the prototype.\"}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc46814c-9be1-4e77-972c-23436738df81","uuid":"466aa3ff-104e-44ae-b31c-9b338e0b70f5","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:39:20.069Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"top\":[{\"id\":\"8:2\",\"name\":\"Start Here · Brief\",\"type\":\"FRAME\",\"w\":1440,\"h\":5164}],\"text\":\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\\n---\\nFoodieland — recipe and food blog website\\n---\\nDesign a recipe website: discover featured and popular recipes, open a recipe with its ingredients and directions, browse and read blog articles, and contact the team. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\\n---\\nHow to work\\n---\\n1. Build exactly the 5 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links.\\n2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions.\\n3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently.\\n4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\\n5. Use the wordmark, the social logos, the photos, the category images, the decorations, the avatars and the icons from 04 · Media.\\n6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\\n---\\nFrames · goals · must include · links\\n---\\nFrame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\\n---\\n01_Home\\n---\\nGoal: Find something to cook today.\\n---\\nMUST INCLUDE\\n---\\n• Categories: “Categories” · “View All Categories” · Breakfast · Vegan · Meat · Dessert · Lunch · Chocolate, each with its image (Category_Breakfast … Category_Chocolate)\\n• Chef promo: “Everyone can be a chef in their own kitchen” · copy (see DATA) · “Learn More” · Photo_Chef · Decor_Tomato · Decor_Onion\\n• Featured recipe: “Hot Recipes” (Icon_Hot_Recipes) · “Spicy delicious chicken wings” · copy (see DATA) · 30 Minutes (Icon_Timer) · Chicken (Icon_Fork_Knife) · Avatar_John_Smith · John Smith · 15 March 2022 · “View Recipes” (Icon_Play) · Photo_Hero_Chicken_Wings · round badge “Handpicked Recipes”\\n• Footer: see DATA (Footer)\\n• Header: Logo_Foodieland · navigation Home / Recipes / Blog / Contact / About us · current: Home · Logo_Facebook · Logo_Twitter · Logo_Instagram\\n• Instagram: “Check out @foodieland on Instagr